# Recorded hangs: mutants that expire on the per-mutant timeout and were never tested.
#
# A TIMED OUT mutant is invisible to every other half of this gate: it is not a kill, it is not a
# survivor, and report.json does not count it in the total. So it cannot become green by silence.
# It is red -- unless the hang is RECORDED HERE, with a ceiling, the same way a survivor is recorded
# in .mutation-allowlist. This file is the difference between "measured, and these are the known
# unmeasurable ones" and "we stopped measuring and called it a day".
#
# Format: one <file> <ceiling> pair per line. The ceiling is the number of expired mutants that
# file may produce in ONE run; anything above it, and any file absent here, is a red verdict.
# A CEILING PER FILE and not an exact set of lines, because expiry is partly contention: the same
# suite reports different hang counts run to run, so pinning lines would fail at random.
#
# EMPTY ON PURPOSE: wsdash has no measured infinite-loop mutant yet. A full-module run
# (make mutate-all) fills this in only with hangs it actually observed.
